1. ABSTRACT

JIP-0608-2 defines a single deterministic system execution architecture replacing fragmented interpretation, governance, and execution layers (Subfolders 3–5).

It establishes a linearized, dependency-safe, non-circular pipeline that enforces strict separation between:

Identity definition

Structural organization

Semantic meaning

Conflict resolution

Governance validation

Execution

State mirroring


This system eliminates bidirectional coupling between subsystems and replaces it with a single forward-execution graph with constrained feedback only through controlled layers.


---

2. DESIGN OBJECTIVE

Primary Goal

Construct a non-ambiguous system execution pipeline where every persistent entity is:

1. Identified (JNL)


2. Structured (JFS / JSL)


3. Defined semantically (JD)


4. Validated for consistency (Resolution Layer)


5. Approved for execution (MIDAS)


6. Executed (GOD SYSTEMS / MCP / AEGIS)


7. Mirrored (JMS)




---

Secondary Goals

Eliminate recursive governance loops

Enforce single-source-of-truth per system layer

Guarantee deterministic traceability for all state transitions

Ensure zero silent mutation across execution stages

Provide strict separation of interpretation vs execution responsibilities



