4. LAYER SPECIFICATIONS


---

4.1 IDENTITY + STRUCTURE LAYER

Components

JNL (Jarvis Navigation Language)

JFS (Jarvis File System)

JSL (Jarvis Structural Layer)


Function

Defines the existence contract of all system entities.

JNL → assigns globally unique identity + address

JFS → defines filesystem placement rules

JSL → enforces structural invariants and hierarchy rules


Formal Behavior

Each entity MUST have:

Unique JNL identifier

Deterministic filesystem location

Valid structural placement under JSL rules


Constraint

This layer is non-semantic and non-executive:

cannot interpret meaning

cannot validate correctness beyond structural compliance



---

4.2 SEMANTIC LAYER (JD — JARVIS DICTIONARY)

Function

Defines meaning only, independent of structure or execution.

Responsibilities

Map JNL identifiers → semantic definitions

Maintain system-wide conceptual consistency

Provide canonical definitions for all system entities


Constraints

JD MUST NOT:

define file structure

define execution rules

define governance policies


JD MUST ONLY:

define meaning

define relationships (semantic, not structural)



---

4.3 RESOLUTION LAYER (CONFLICT ARBITRATION ENGINE)

Function

Acts as a deterministic reconciliation engine between:

JNL identity

JFS/JSL structure

JD semantics


Responsibilities

Detect mismatches between identity and meaning

Resolve ambiguous references

Normalize inconsistent mappings

Produce canonical interpretation state for downstream validation


Input Types

Structural inconsistencies (JFS/JSL mismatch)

Semantic conflicts (JD ambiguity)

Identity collisions (JNL duplication or drift)


Output

A resolved system state object (RSO) containing:

canonical reference mapping

validated entity relationships

corrected alignment graph


Constraint

Resolution Layer is:

deterministic

non-executive

non-governance


It does NOT approve actions.


---

4.4 GOVERNANCE LAYER (MIDAS)

Function

MIDAS is the pre-execution constraint validator enforcing all system-wide invariants.

Responsibilities

Enforce Gold Laws (GL2–GL10 + extensions)

Validate structural integrity

Validate JNL compliance

Validate JD consistency

Validate Resolution Layer output

Reject non-compliant execution requests


Output States

ALLOW → passes execution forward

WARN → non-critical anomaly detected

BLOCK → execution forbidden

REPAIR → suggests minimal correction path


Constraint

MIDAS MUST NOT:

interpret semantics

execute operations

modify system state directly


It is a stateless validation gate only.


---

4.5 EXECUTION LAYER (GOD SYSTEMS / AEGIS / MCP)

Function

Executes validated operations from MIDAS.

Responsibilities

tool invocation (MCP)

system action execution (AEGIS)

workflow routing (GOD SYSTEMS)

external system interaction (GitHub / Supabase / APIs)


Constraint

Execution Layer MUST NOT:

validate correctness

interpret meaning

modify governance rules


It only executes approved instructions.


---

4.6 MIRROR LAYER (JMS — JARVIS MIRROR SYSTEM)

Function

Maintains a non-authoritative replication of system state.

Responsibilities

IndexSummary updates

system state synchronization

cross-repository consistency mapping

traceability logging


Constraint

JMS MUST NEVER:

generate truth

modify data semantics

resolve conflicts

trigger execution


It is strictly reflective.


